module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Rig.HenselizationDescent

/-!
# The map out of a henselization into a henselian pair

The henselization `(Aʰ, Iʰ)` of a pair `(A, I)` is initial among henselian pairs under
`(A, I)`. This file names the map that initiality provides: for an `A`-algebra `C` and an
ideal `L ⊆ C` such that `(C, L)` is henselian and `I` lands in `L`, there is a canonical
`A`-algebra map `Aʰ → C`, it carries `I·Aʰ` into `L`, and it is the only `A`-algebra map
`Aʰ → C`.

## Main definitions

* `henselizationLift`: the canonical `A`-algebra map from the henselization of the pair
  `(A, I)` to a henselian pair `(C, L)` under it.

## Main results

* `henselizationLift_map_le_comap`: the canonical map carries `I·Aʰ` into `L`.
* `henselizationLift_unique`: it is the *only* `A`-algebra map `Aʰ → C`. No compatibility with
  the ideals is assumed, because an `A`-algebra map satisfies it automatically.

## Implementation notes

The universal property of the canonical `henselization A I`, as opposed to that of an unnamed
witness, is `henselization_universalProperty`. It produces a ring homomorphism; the
`A`-algebra structure of the lift is its compatibility with the structure map of the
henselization, which is the first half of the recorded property. Since that universal property
is available for targets in the universe of `A`, so is this lift.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A02](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A02)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

/-- The canonical `A`-algebra map from the henselization of the pair `(A, I)` to an
`A`-algebra `C` carrying `I` into an ideal `L` for which `(C, L)` is a henselian pair. -/
noncomputable def henselizationLift (A : Type u) {C : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing C]
    [Algebra A C] (I : Ideal A) (L : Ideal C) (hL : HenselianPair C L)
    (hIL : I ≤ L.comap (algebraMap A C)) :
    (henselization A I : Type u) →ₐ[A] C where
  toRingHom := Classical.choose
    (henselization_universalProperty A I C inferInstance L hL (algebraMap A C) hIL)
  commutes' a := DFunLike.congr_fun (Classical.choose_spec
    (henselization_universalProperty A I C inferInstance L hL (algebraMap A C) hIL)).1.1 a

/-- The canonical map out of the henselization of `(A, I)` carries the ideal generated by `I`
into the henselian ideal of the target. -/
theorem henselizationLift_map_le_comap (A : Type u) {C : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing C]
    [Algebra A C] (I : Ideal A) (L : Ideal C) (hL : HenselianPair C L)
    (hIL : I ≤ L.comap (algebraMap A C)) :
    I.map (algebraMap A (henselization A I : Type u)) ≤
      L.comap (henselizationLift A I L hL hIL).toRingHom :=
  (Classical.choose_spec
    (henselization_universalProperty A I C inferInstance L hL (algebraMap A C) hIL)).1.2

/-- The canonical map out of the henselization of `(A, I)` is the only `A`-algebra map into a
henselian pair `(C, L)` under `(A, I)`: compatibility with the ideals is automatic for an
`A`-algebra map, so uniqueness in the universal property applies to every one of them. -/
theorem henselizationLift_unique (A : Type u) {C : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing C]
    [Algebra A C] (I : Ideal A) (L : Ideal C) (hL : HenselianPair C L)
    (hIL : I ≤ L.comap (algebraMap A C)) (g : (henselization A I : Type u) →ₐ[A] C) :
    g = henselizationLift A I L hL hIL := by
  apply AlgHom.coe_ringHom_injective
  have hg : g.toRingHom.comp (algebraMap A (henselization A I : Type u)) = algebraMap A C := by
    ext a
    exact g.commutes a
  have hgi : I.map (algebraMap A (henselization A I : Type u)) ≤ L.comap g.toRingHom := by
    rw [Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap]
    intro a ha
    show g (algebraMap A (henselization A I : Type u) a) ∈ L
    simpa only [Ideal.mem_comap, g.commutes] using hIL ha
  have h := (Classical.choose_spec
    (henselization_universalProperty A I C inferInstance L hL (algebraMap A C) hIL)).2
    g.toRingHom ⟨hg, hgi⟩
  show g.toRingHom = (henselizationLift A I L hL hIL).toRingHom
  exact h

end
